-- title:
--   The $71$-torsion kernel admits the required two-character filtration
-- statement:
--   Let $V=ker(π)$, let $ψ$ be the order-five character, and let $χ_{71}$ be the mod-$71$ cyclotomic character. There exist Galois-equivariant homomorphisms $i:𝔽_{71}(ψ)→V$ and $q:V→𝔽_{71}(χ_{71})$ such that $i$ is injective, $q$ is surjective, and $ker(q)=im(i)$: $$0→𝔽_{71}(ψ)\xrightarrow{i}V\xrightarrow{q}𝔽_{71}(χ_{71})→0.$$ This provides the exact kernel filtration used throughout the global descent.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

